Explicitly unmute the voice transmit path

HYPOTHESIS: the microphone is neither broken nor badly routed, it is MUTED in
the DSP.

Downstream, after starting voice, sends an explicit mute for each direction
(VSS_IVOLUME_CMD_MUTE_V2, with VSS_IVOLUME_DIRECTION_RX/TX). The ported q6voice
sends none and takes for granted that the DSP starts up unmuted.

If it does not, exactly the picture we had comes out, point by point:

  - The voice session is created without A SINGLE error; every MVM and CVP
    command answers ok.
  - Reception is heard perfectly.
  - The microphone reaches the DSP port: the 491 registers of the TX macro and
    the 413 of the codec are BYTE FOR BYTE identical when recording (works) and
    in a call (does not work).
  - The transmit port starts and is triggered (TX Capture in RUNNING).
  - And nothing arrives at the other end.

It is a much simpler explanation than the one about the ACDB topologies, and it
needs no shared memory, no touching the boot path, and no calibration: it is
one more command in the call's start-up sequence.

BOTH directions are unmuted. Reception already worked, so if it kept working
after this, it also confirms that the command is accepted.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c	2026-08-11 13:47:57.620524295 +0200
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c	2026-08-11 13:48:20.453643161 +0200
@@ -26,6 +26,17 @@
 
 #define VSS_ICOMMON_CAL_NETWORK_ID_NONE			0x0001135E
 
+#define VSS_IVOLUME_CMD_MUTE_V2				0x0001138B
+#define VSS_IVOLUME_DIRECTION_RX			0
+#define VSS_IVOLUME_DIRECTION_TX			1
+
+struct vss_ivolume_cmd_mute_v2_cmd {
+	struct apr_hdr hdr;
+	u16 direction;
+	u16 mute_flag;
+	u16 ramp_duration_ms;
+} __packed;
+
 #define VSS_IVOCPROC_CMD_ENABLE				0x000100C6
 #define VSS_IVOCPROC_CMD_DISABLE			0x000110E1
 
@@ -291,6 +302,29 @@
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6cvp_send_media_format);
 
+/*
+ * Downstream, tras arrancar la voz, manda un mute EXPLICITO por cada
+ * direccion. El q6voice portado no mandaba ninguno, y si el DSP arranca la
+ * transmision muteada eso da exactamente el cuadro que teniamos: la sesion se
+ * crea sin un solo error, se oye al otro extremo, el microfono llega al puerto
+ * del DSP... y al otro lado no llega nada.
+ */
+int q6cvp_set_mute(struct q6voice_session *cvp, bool tx, bool mute)
+{
+	struct vss_ivolume_cmd_mute_v2_cmd cmd;
+
+	cmd.hdr.pkt_size = sizeof(cmd);
+	cmd.hdr.opcode = VSS_IVOLUME_CMD_MUTE_V2;
+
+	cmd.direction = tx ? VSS_IVOLUME_DIRECTION_TX
+			   : VSS_IVOLUME_DIRECTION_RX;
+	cmd.mute_flag = mute;
+	cmd.ramp_duration_ms = 0;
+
+	return q6voice_common_send(cvp, &cmd.hdr);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6cvp_set_mute);
+
